From bfacb0f7effeb54f797b3c33b87a480b10f3e5bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:56:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] cheeseburger: WLAN copy engines + HTC after mission mode (W5
 part 1)

0151 test A froze the SoC 12 s after WLAN_MODE mission, test B (stop at FW_READY) ran 60 s clean: the firmware wants the host copy engines that ath10k_snoc_hif_power_up programs right after wlan_enable. sweet_wce.c ports topaz 0123 CE + HTC (TopazModem.cpp, APSL 2.0): CE regs at membase 0x18800000 + 0x240000, shadow write indices at +0x32000, RRI in DDR, rings and 32 x 2 KiB rx buffers per pipe from the modem pool (physical addresses through the ANOC2 identity bank). Started 100 ms after WLAN_MODE ok (kern.sweetwlfw_upto 0 with the SMMU bank), polled from the watch loop; HTC READY -> connect HTT then WMI -> SETUP_COMPLETE_EX; WMI events only logged (INIT/scan are part 2). upto 3 = mission without CE (0151 behaviour). CE/HTC summary every 5 s.
